TASK DESCRIPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Objective: Design and implement new backend API endpoints required to power
             a web-based CIRO Command Dashboard for hackathon judge demonstration.
             The dashboard must show the complete multi-agent pipeline working
             from start to end — active incidents, agent states, live logs, and
             tactical actions.

  Scope    :
    1. Read and understand the full project architecture (all endpoints, agents,
       models, tools, frontend screens).
    2. Audit existing APIs and identify what is already available.
    3. Identify gaps in the API surface that prevent a complete dashboard view.
    4. Design and implement 3 new dashboard endpoints.
    5. Register the new router in the main API file.
    6. Write and run tests to verify all 3 new endpoints return HTTP 200.
    7. Analyze and document remaining gaps for future tasks.

